		{"id":"564ec3aa730c0829","type":"text","text":"![[image-21.png]]","x":3733,"y":2400,"width":560,"height":580},
		{"id":"3422870b168115e9","type":"text","text":"\n| Tracts                     | Functions                                                                                                                                                     |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Tectospinal Tract**      | Turning of Head & Eye movements                                                                                                                               |\n| **Rubrospinal Tract**      | α-flexor tone in distal parts                                                                                                                                 |\n|                            | **Dominant descending pathways** in lower animals                                                                                                             |\n| **Reticulospinal Tracts**  | **Pontine -** Stimulatory to γ-extensors of medial antigravity m.s                                                                                            |\n|                            | **Medullary -** Inhibitory to γ-extensors of medial antigravity m.s                                                                                           |\n|                            | Pontine Tracts are more dominant than Medullary Tracts                                                                                                        |\n| **Vestibulospinal Tracts** | **Lateral -** Descends *ipsilaterally through the entire spinal cord. <br>Responsible for α-extensor tone of axial m.s                                        |\n|                            | **Medial -** Descends *bilaterally* to cervical & upper thoracic levels <br>Coordinate Head & Neck movements w/ eye movements via [[Vestibulo-ocular Reflex]] |\n| **Olivospinal Tract**      | Cervical & Upper limb α-flexor tone                                                                                                                           |\n\n","x":4423,"y":2400,"width":690,"height":580},
		{"id":"3a361058437d2651","type":"text","text":"\n| Commisural Fibres               | Parts of Brain connected                                                                |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Ant. Commisure                  | Olfactory bulbs and olfactory cortices <br>Temporal Lobes (esp. Amygdaloid bodies)      |\n| Post. Commisure                 | Pretectal nuclei, Edinger–Westphal nuclei, and other midbrain pupillary reflex centres. |\n| Habenular Commisure             | Habenular nuclei (part of the epithalamus)                                              |\n| Hippocampal Commisure           | Hippocampal formations and fornices                                                     |\n| Interthalamic Adhesion          | Medial thalami                                                                          |\n| Collicular Adhesions (Midbrain) | Superior & Inferior Colliculi                                                           |\n","x":3520,"y":-579,"width":520,"height":389},
		{"id":"33ba061f44eef90f","type":"text","text":"#### Minor - Spino-olivary Tracts & Dorsolateral Tracts","x":-463,"y":1380,"width":343,"height":80},
